  "enable": false,
  "reason": "every bank-tile input lands in RTL pin flops (beat landing v/beat/data, the stage's descriptor/partial-sum seam flops, the write-port flops wv_q/xv_q/j_q/wa_q in ot_hbm_hc_bank_static, feed registers) and every output is a flop (stage SOR seam register, feed registers, wfault); a kit flop stage would shift the compiled systolic schedule"
 },
 "structural_change": "HBM-COLLECT10/HCE2 10-21 e2rw7: e2_rw4 (91d749022, ep9) FAILED CTS: clk_c boundary pin-flop spread 432.1 ps TT (60 boundary of 291 sinks: cd[0]/cv[0] at the W in-face d_* pins vs cd[8]/cv[8] at the E out-face o_* pins, plus fin_q / f_o at the NW / NE corners); e2_rw4c (clk_c folded into clk) clk 461.7. One root over a ~730 um register chain: a pin move cannot fix it. rw7 = 10-20 CLOCK RULE region split: W region clk_c (chain stages 0..5) and E region clk_ce (out registers) joined by a D4/K2 mesochronous landing ring (ot_pl_land_w/_r, offset at reset, no flow control) that replaces chain stages 6..8 (0 added edges); f flag W->E through a D4/K1 ring (clk_w3 -> clk_x3, 0 added edges, the centre samples f with leaf_v); x SRAM write copies on clk_x<h> (no root spans the W weight column and the E x column); STG 1 per-row stage-control copies (rw5). MAIN: row-0/1 clock entries (clk_w/d/e/x 0..1) moved to the S face free segments beside their row masses; clk_c / clk_ce on S beside the chain.",
